Algorithm: Library Management System

1. Start the program.
2. Declare a structure to store book ID, title, author, total copies, and issued copies.
3. Display the main menu.
4. Read the user’s choice.
5. If the user selects Add Book, read book details and store them in the array.
6. If the user selects Display Books, display all stored book records.
7. If the user selects Issue Book, search for the book ID and check availability. If a copy is available, increase the issued count.
8. If the user selects Return Book, search for the ID and decrease the issued count if a copy was issued.
9. If the user selects Sort Books, arrange the records alphabetically by title using bubble sort.
10. Execute the selected algorithm or C programming demonstration when requested.
11. Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
12. Stop the program.
